{
  "_id": 23056,
  "id": "the_finale_of_a_lie",
  "name": "The Finale of a Lie",
  "desc": "\"What did Introduction to Detective Deduction say again? Unless absolutely necessary...\"\nFangs woven in red and black crept inch by inch up his shoulder.\n\nWhere the night drowns deepest, clouds of doubt emerge. In the shadowed forest, vicious beasts lurk.\n\"This game of cat and mouse... it's time to end it.\"\nThe crimson fades. Moonlight still gleams silver across the sky, and the stars rest in peaceful slumber.\n\nThis is yet another one of his searches for the truth, but the shadows of the past tap his shoulder, then dissipate into nothing.\nThe maneuvering of this very moment continues, until—\n\n\"Until... the day retribution falls upon the wicked.\"",
  "rarity": 5,
  "pathType": "Rogue",
  "pathTypeText": "The Hunt",
  "effectName": "Subsume",
  "effectTemplate": "Increases the wearer's CRIT Rate by <color=#f29e38ff>#1[i]%</color>. At the start of battle or for every #2[i] instance(s) of Follow-Up ATK the wearer uses, the wearer gains \"Umbra Devourer,\" lasting for #3[i] turn(s). While the wearer holds \"Umbra Devourer,\" increases ATK by <color=#f29e38ff>#4[i]%</color> and increases the DMG taken by all enemies by <color=#f29e38ff>#5[i]%</color>. Effects of the same type cannot stack.",
